From 1d6ef26d412170c44454dedf3518716cdb6f5af9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen De Vleeschauwer <kdv@kdvelectronics.eu>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 14:24:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] speedtest: Add the mon speedtest command

Backport of speedtest from blackmagic-rtthread (18e2b30b).

`mon speedtest [COUNT [SIZE [ADDR]]]` (default 16 writes of 1024 bytes to
the start of target RAM) times SWD/JTAG writes to target RAM and reports
the throughput. The overwritten RAM is backed up beforehand, the written
data is verified, and the RAM is restored afterwards.

Firmware specific changes:
- Timing uses the millisecond counter refined with the probe's SysTick
  count, for microsecond resolution (RT-Thread ticks before); BMDA
  falls back to milliseconds.
- The firmware printf family has no 64-bit support, so results are
  printed from 32-bit values and COUNT * SIZE must fit in 32 bits.
- speedtest.c is built for the firmware and BMDA, as command.c, which
  registers the command, is shared.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
